    {
      "id": "c-glaze",
      "name": "Cone 6 glaze chemistry",
      "topic": "Mid-fire recipe troubleshooting. Post the recipe and the fired result together or nobody can help you.",
      "tags": [
        "ceramics",
        "glaze-chemistry",
        "cone:6"
      ],
      "listed": true,
      "matching": "inclusive",
      "kind": "conversation",
      "myRole": "member",
      "otherOwnerCount": 2,
      "memberCount": 34,
      "canPost": true,
      "messages": [
        {
          "id": "m-201",
          "authorId": "id-noor",
          "at": "2026-08-01T10:10:00Z",
          "time": "10:10 AM",
          "text": "Getting crawling on a satin matte at cone 6, worst on vertical surfaces. Recipe is 40 neph sy, 20 silica, 20 whiting, 20 EPK.",
          "reactions": []
        },
        {
          "id": "m-202",
          "authorId": "id-desmond",
          "at": "2026-08-01T10:26:00Z",
          "time": "10:26 AM",
          "text": "20% EPK is doing it. Raw clay shrinks as it dries and pulls the glaze apart before it ever melts. Calcine half of it and the crawling usually stops dead.",
          "reactions": [
            {
              "emoji": "✅",
              "identityIds": [
                "id-noor",
                "id-priya"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "m-203",
          "authorId": "id-priya",
          "at": "2026-08-01T10:41:00Z",
          "time": "10:41 AM",
          "text": "@noor-h Also worth checking how long the pots sat between bisque and glazing. Dust on a bisque surface will do the same thing and it is a much cheaper fix than reformulating.",
          "reactions": [
            {
              "emoji": "👍",
              "identityIds": [
                "id-desmond"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "m-204",
          "authorId": "id-noor",
          "at": "2026-08-01T11:15:00Z",
          "time": "11:15 AM",
          "text": "They sat about three weeks on an open shelf. That is probably the whole story.",
          "reactions": []
        },
        {
          "id": "m-205",
          "authorId": "id-oskar",
          "at": "2026-08-01T11:58:00Z",
          "time": "11:58 AM",
          "text": "Rinse and let them dry overnight before you glaze. I stopped losing pots to crawling entirely once I started doing that.",
          "reactions": [
            {
              "emoji": "🙏",
              "identityIds": [
                "id-noor"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "m-206",
          "authorId": "id-desmond",
          "at": "2026-08-01T12:05:00Z",
          "time": "12:05 PM",
          "text": "If it is still crawling after that, post the fired result and we can work out whether it is application thickness instead.",
          "reactions": []
        }
      ],
      "participants": [
        "id-noor",
        "id-desmond",
        "id-priya",
        "id-oskar"
      ]
    },
