          "id": "m-501",
          "authorId": "id-oskar",
          "at": "2026-07-29T08:30:00Z",
          "time": "8:30 AM",
          "text": "Six weeks in and I still cannot centre more than two pounds without it going off. What actually fixed this for you?",
          "reactions": []
        },
        {
          "id": "m-502",
          "authorId": "id-marisol",
          "at": "2026-07-29T08:52:00Z",
          "time": "8:52 AM",
          "text": "Brace your forearm against your hip and stop moving your hands. Centring is a bracing problem, not a strength problem.",
          "reactions": [
            {
              "emoji": "🔥",
              "identityIds": [
                "id-oskar",
                "id-noor"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "m-503",
          "authorId": "id-junie",
          "at": "2026-07-29T09:20:00Z",
          "time": "9:20 AM",
          "text": "And wetter than you think for the first thirty seconds. Most people fight dry clay and blame themselves.",
          "reactions": [
            {
              "emoji": "👍",
              "identityIds": [
                "id-oskar"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "m-504",
          "authorId": "id-oskar",
          "at": "2026-07-29T09:41:00Z",
          "time": "9:41 AM",
          "text": "Bracing against the hip did it. Three pounds centred first try this morning.",
